# Files and directories excluded from the wordpress.org SVN push. The
# canonical SVN tag should contain only what end users need to install the
# plugin — no test fixtures, CI infrastructure, or dev-only source assets.
#
# Used by 10up/action-wordpress-plugin-deploy and `rsync --filter` workflows.

# VCS / CI
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.distignore

# Tests + dev tooling
tests
scripts
node_modules
vendor
phpcs.xml
phpcs.xml.dist
phpunit.xml
phpunit.xml.dist
package.json
package-lock.json
composer.json
composer.lock

# Source / authoring assets (the runtime icons under assets/img/ are shipped)
Stealth_Access_Logo.png

# WordPress.org listing assets — these live in the SVN /assets/ directory
# (handled separately by 10up/action-wordpress-plugin-deploy) and must NOT
# ship inside the installable plugin folder.
.wordpress-org

# Local-only audit + release docs (gitignored, but exclude defensively in
# case anyone runs a dist build with these in the working tree).
Security_Audit.md
Medium_Findings_Prioritization.md
Release_Readiness_Report.md
Release_Preparation_Report.md
Release_Package_Report.md

# Build / test output
playwright-report
playwright-results
test-results
artifacts

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
